  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HIV/AIDS - Algeria (01-Jan-2017-31-Dec-2019)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Algeria, HIV, Ministry of Health, Population and Hospital Reform of the People&apos;s Democratic Republic of Algeria ()This program has the following goals: Reduce the number of new infections.  Reduce the various forms of HIV-related stigma and discrimination.  Stabilize the mortality rate specific to HIV. The objectives of this program are: At least 90% of the populations most exposed to the risk of infection (SWs, MSM, people who inject drugs) adopt attitudes and practices that reduce the risk of HIV transmission.  At least 90% of vulnerable populations (youth, women, mobile populations, PDL, men in uniform) adopt attitudes and practices that protect them from the risk of HIV infection</narrative>
  </description>
